              "waypoints": [
                {
                  "id": "w2",
                  "title": "Modified `<CartPage />` to render a heading with the totals",
                  "declaration": "CartPage",
                  "reading": "The author modified a component `<CartPage />` that now returns an `<h1>` above the `<ul>` of the items, such as `2 items for $24.00`, where its `<section>` had no heading before. `itemCount` and `totalCents` are the result of [`useCartTotals()`](code:src/hooks/use-cart-totals.ts#useCartTotals), which [returns both from the cart store](code:src/hooks/use-cart-totals.ts#L6). [`formatQuantity(1)` returns `1 item`](code:src/lib/format.ts#L9-11) and [`formatPrice(2400)` returns `$24.00`](code:src/lib/format.ts#L5-7). The call of `useCartTotals()` is before the `if` that returns `<p>Your cart is empty.</p>`, so the hook runs for a cart with no items too, and that cart still gets the message and no heading. [`<CartSummary />` still reads `selectTotalCents` itself](code:src/routes/cart/components/CartSummary.tsx#L7) and [renders `Total:` with the price](code:src/routes/cart/components/CartSummary.tsx#L18), so the page shows the total in the heading and below the list.",
                  "needsAttention": "This is the one place where the pull request changes what a shopper sees: `<CartPage />` [renders an `<h1>` with the item count and the total](code:src/routes/cart/index.tsx#L13-15) for a cart with items. The other three waypoints add [`useCartTotals()`](code:src/hooks/use-cart-totals.ts#useCartTotals) and the imports that the heading uses.",
